## Chapter 3: Safety, Privacy, and Sensory Edge Processing## 3-1. Zero-Camera Framework for absolute Privacy Protection

* Eliminates all optical camera arrays from the hardware architecture. Spatial awareness and obstacle avoidance are executed solely by decentralized non-visual sensors (thermal sensors, infrared, millimeter-wave radar, and LiDAR) that are incapable of identifying individual privacy assets.

## 3-2. Personal Identification & Substance Detection Systems (Sensory Edge Processing)

* Voice (Acoustic Identification): Audio wave inputs captured by left and right microphones undergo local, lightweight Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) analysis inside the MCU to authenticate the registered owner based on frequency characteristics (voiceprints).
* Chemical/Odor Pattern Matching:
Reads chemical sensor surface resistance variations as analog voltage values. Volatile Organic Compounds (VOCs) originating from the registered owner's unique body odor, silver vine extract (nepetalactone), or dog treat amino acids are matched locally against pre-registered gas concentration waveform templates.
* Sensor Latency Compensation via Behavioral Buffering:
To mask the multi-second time delay required for chemical sensors to analyze odors, the system avoids mechanical lock-ups. Instead, it automatically cues realistic animal animations—such as "sniffing around" or "twitching ears to listen"—transforming technical processing latency into biological realism.

## 3-3. Thermal Sensor-Cleaning (Odor Refresh) Mechanism

* Upon concluding a detection routine or returning to the charging dock, the system activates miniature internal heating elements within the chemical sensor housing for a few seconds. This thermal burst rapidly evaporates bound odor molecules, resetting the sensor surface and eliminating residual scent contamination.

